  "findings": [
    "LifeEventTile#getMinX/getMaxX uses the resulting level in IGNORE_FUTURE_ACTIVATE mode; positive levels contribute center-5 and center+level*5. Rust adds a lifecycle-variation scan and feeds these bounds to each enclosing group. The arithmetic is supported by Java source.",
    "The scan only sees accepted legacy-style variations, not the full Java LifeEvent/message callback history. LifeEventTile has zero preferred height, LiveBoxes#getStairs samples per-event levels and resets ownership across standalone notes, and Stairs#addStep discards decreasing ordinates. Rust retains the30-unit same-message row and pairs opens/closes. Eight new cases fail;22/24 original maker cases also fail and are copied byte-for-byte into this mechanism standing corpus.",
    "Example primary Java height422 versus Rust452. A correct horizontal bounds helper is insufficient when the event/stair data supplying its level and placement is incomplete. All22 maker failures plus eight new failures are named in this record; no scope waiver is applied.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
